From 82beb709027eb4e26b74b3628198816e40c188fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qualcomm-toolbox <169756160+qcom-toolbox@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 23:13:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 202/202] umi: the QCA6390 as the station and en0 link for
 wifid

ios-flame's flame_sta.c glues the station boundary to its userland
radio; umi's radio is in the kernel, so bsd/dev/sweet_wlsta.c glues it
to sweet_wlce.c / sweet_wldp.c. After stage 8's first scan,
sweet_wlce_htc hands over to it (boot-arg sweetwifid, default 1;
sweetwifid=0 keeps the kernel's own join + DHCP + en0 of 0140-0154):
en0 comes from redwood_net.c with the link down, the station is
attached, and the boot line's sweetwlanssid becomes a standing join
request. configd's DHCP runs on en0 once the link is up.

sweet_wlce.c:
- the BSS table keeps signal (snr + ATH11K_DEFAULT_NOISE_FLOOR -95,
  ath11k wmi.c), beacon interval, capability, elements and last-heard
  time, refreshed by every beacon; a full table gives up the oldest;
- START_SCAN is its own function (wmi_start_scan), the association its
  own (wlce_assoc: strongest BSS with that name, state reset first);
- leave: deauth (reason 3), VDEV_DOWN 0x5007/tag 0x5e, PEER_DELETE
  0x6002/0x62 -> 0x6007, VDEV_STOP 0x5006/0x5d -> 0x5002 (ath11k
  wmi.h v6.12, ath11k_bss_disassoc / ath11k_mac_vdev_stop order);
- link loss: deauth/disassoc to us, PEER_STA_KICKOUT 0x6001, ROAM
  0xb001 reason 2 (beacon miss);
- wlce_lock shared by the net thread's poll, transmit and the station
  thread; waits drop it while they sleep.

Open networks on 2.4 GHz only, as the radio is today; a WPA join is
refused with EAUTH. While joined a real scan runs at most every 20 s.
With the station, the IO80211Controller entries come with en0 instead
of at AppleCLCD start (sweetwlanearly=1 forces the early publish).

